.git
docs

# Operational data and secrets must never reach the build context (and so never an image layer).
# Real env files: everything named .env, .env.* or *.env, except the checked-in *.example templates.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example
!**/*.env.example
# The work package (deploy/work) and the self-hosted profile (deploy/selfhost) write their
# generated secrets, backups and logs next to their compose files.
deploy/work/secrets
deploy/work/backups
deploy/work/work.env
deploy/work/*.log
deploy/selfhost/secrets
deploy/selfhost/backups
deploy/selfhost/update-state
deploy/selfhost/ntfy-secrets
deploy/selfhost/Caddyfile
**/secrets
**/backups
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.log

# Dependencies, build output and caches
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pyright
**/.mypy_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.vite
**/.cache
